      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.  Availble in java.lang\n\n2. allows to change the content of object without creating new Object .\n\nConstructors\n============\n\n1. StringBuffer ( ) --> creates a empty StringBuffer object of capacity\n16 .\n\n2. StringBuffer (int ) --> accepts int and creates an empty StringBuffer\nof capacity=value provided .\n\n3. StringBuffer(String s) --> Accepts an String and creates a\nStringBuffer object of capacity= size of String provided + 16 .\n\nMethods of StringBuffer\n======================\n\n1. capacity() --> returns the capacity of StringBuffer object .\n\n2. length() --> returns the number of character in StringBuffer .\n\n3. append( .. ) --> accepts any type of arguement and adds it at the\nend of StringBuffer object if the capacity is full the new capacity is\ngenerated that is 2*curr_cap +2 .\n\n4. delete(int start , int end )--> delete characters from start index to\nend-1 index .\n\n5. reverse() --> revese the character of StringBuffer in place .\n\n6. replace(int start, int end , String) --> replace the string from start\nindex to end-1 index with given String .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.  Availble in java.lang\n\n2. allows to change the content of object without creating new Object .\n\nConstructors\n============\n\n1. StringBuffer ( ) --> creates a empty StringBuffer object of capacity 16 .\n\n2. StringBuffer (int ) --> accepts int and creates an empty StringBuffer of capacity=value provided .\n\n3. StringBuffer(String s) --> Accepts an String and creates a StringBuffer object of capacity= size of String provided + 16 .\n\nMethods of StringBuffer\n======================\n\n1. capacity() --> returns the capacity of StringBuffer object .\n\n2. length() --> returns the number of character in StringBuffer .\n\n3. append( .. ) --> accepts any type of arguement and adds it at the end of StringBuffer object if the capacity is full the new capacity is generated that is 2*curr_cap +2 .\n\n4. delete(int start , int end )--> delete characters from start index to end-1 index .\n\n5. reverse() --> revese the character of StringBuffer in place .\n\n6. replace(int start, int end , String) --> replace the string from start index to end-1 index with given String .",
